BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around Taylor Memorial
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T153000
UID:69a1fcf81e64afd01e5e8f7a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Taylor Memorial Branch and its neighbourhood is home to a var
 iety of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore th
 e natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize diff
 erent species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance
 .\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nRegistrat
 ion is required\nThe tour will start and end at the Taylor Memorial meetin
 g room and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. Th
 ere may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and pre
 pare accordingly for this outdoor program  (hats\, sunscreen\, water\, co
 mfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of 
 severe inclement weather\, registrants will be notified of an alternative 
 date.
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a1fcf81e64afd01e5e8f7a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
