BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Henna Art Workshop for Children
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T150000
UID:69e12d52bd9a3c316a535868@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Asian Heritage Month and discover the art of henna\,
  decorative designs which are created on a person's body\, using a paste o
 f natural organic henna. Observe and enjoy the henna application and lear
 n about its history\, recipe and traditions. Led by Henna Artist\, Hina Ya
 sir.\nDrop In. Space is limited.\nPlease Note: Henna will be available on 
 a first-come\, first-served basis. The final henna application will begin 
 no later than 2:55 pm. No new designs will be started after this time.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e12d52bd9a3c316a535868
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
