BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mimico Kids & Parents Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T160000
UID:69e24a6bfca21471b7ef7aee@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Our book for May is Grimm's Fairy Tales by Jakob & Wilhelm Gri
 mm. First published in 1812\, these timeless stories have enchanted genera
 tions of children. Some of the stories are scary\, some whimsical\, but al
 l are spellbinding and have had a huge influence down through the years. T
 hese stories first introduced characters such as Hansel and Gretel\, Rapun
 zel\, Tom Thumb\, and many more.\nCopies available at the library.\nGrimm'
 s Fairy Tales
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e24a6bfca21471b7ef7aee
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:KatzTollar play the Jewish-Themed Music of Brian Katz
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T130000
UID:69e7f02b213814b1b5249f45@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This suite of Brian Katz’s Jewish-themed compositions are in
 spired by contrasting life events such as meditating in an olive grove out
 side of Jerusalem\; spontaneously creating a Celtic-Klezmer piece in the s
 hower and dreaming a nigun (wordless melody) while staying in a hotel—pa
 cked with Rabbi’s—in Elora\, Ontario.\nKatzTollar\n(Brian Katz\, guita
 r\, voice\; Ernie Tollar\, sax\, bansuri flute\, ney) are widely known for
  their ability to synthesize diverse styles into a voice of their own.\nOf
  “Leaves Will Speak\,”\nBrian Katz\n\, solo guitar\, music critic\, St
 anley Fefferman of Opus 1 Reviews writes: “The whole vibe is Brian’s o
 wn blend of classical\, medieval\, Spanish\, Jazz\, Blues\, finger-picking
  Folk\, Greek\, Middle Eastern and Klezmer— you can hear all those threa
 ds in the weave of this album’s harmonic fabric. You can enjoy the play 
 of musical intelligence on this album and dig into a rich horde of experie
 nce gathered along the way of Brian’s 30-year international career.” J
 azz Podium\, Germany wrote of Brian: “If you want music that speaks\, he
 re it is.”\nErnie Tollar\nperformed his first professional gigs at age 1
 6 and has since toured Europe\, India\, Egypt\, Kapuskasing\, U.S.A.\, Arg
 entina\, Mexico\, and Canada. He has performed and recorded with an incred
 ible array of distinguished artists including Holly Cole\, Kenny Wheeler\,
  Trichy Sankaran\, Joe Lovano\, Maze Mazé\, Space Trio\, as well as sever
 al bands with his wife\, vocalist Maryem Tollar\; their collaborative 2009
  recording\, “Cairo to Toronto\,” garnered them a JUNO award nominatio
 n.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e7f02b213814b1b5249f45
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pawsitively Pets: Hands-on Animal Education
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T140000
UID:69f922a8caf934360059c572@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pawsitively Pets is a hands-on animal education program for ch
 ildren of all ages. Our wonderful animal team is made up of an assortment 
 of rescued pets that have found their forever home with us. Our goal is to
  provide our animal team with a permanent home and the best possible care\
 , while sharing our love or animals with others. All programs focus on res
 ponsible pet ownership\, and the life-long commitment of owning a pet.\nPl
 ease note this program is suitable for children 6 years old up with adult 
 accompaniment. This program is meant for children to attend with their adu
 lts or caregiver.\nWhen signing up please indicate how many CHILDREN are a
 ttending\n. One adult may attend per child\, but the adult does not need t
 o register.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room. Lower Level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f922a8caf934360059c572
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
