BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Water - Relay Educations STEM Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T153000
UID:69fa8222177319280017b987@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Dive into our waterways and learn how we use water for drinkin
 g\, sanitation\, energy\, and more. We talk about Indigenous understanding
 s of water\, and how cities and rural areas manage water supply in Canada.
 \nThis workshop highlights the importance of the hydrological cycle. The h
 ydrological cycle describes the movement and flow of water on Earth\, and 
 involves different stages such as evaporation\, condensation\, and precipi
 tation. We also discuss climate change strategies and population impacts i
 n different regions.\nStudents will conduct experiments using water to get
  an electric current and more!
LOCATION:Bendale\, Auditorium - Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa8222177319280017b987
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
