BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After School Role-Playing Games: Mausritter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T170000
UID:69ce83c82866a5b48845f761@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:As mice who seek adventure in a vast and dangerous world\, wil
 l our simple weapons and homemade armour be enough to protect us from the 
 claws and fangs of hungry snakes cats and spiders? Probably not.\nWill a 
 well-timed spell help? Maybe a little.\nWhat you will need is imagination
 \, strategy and teamwork!\nMausritter\nis a swords and whiskers role-playi
 ng game in the vein of classic stories such as\nMouse Guard\nand\nRedwal\n
 l. The stakes are high but there is perilous combat\, sneaky plans\, treas
 ure and a chance to become the heroes of your meadow. Some mice will lose 
 their lives (heroically of course)\, but you as the player can just get a 
 new mouse and keep on playing.\nWe will be running two tables of up to six
  players each so space is limited. Please register soon!\n*Registration is
  required. Ages 8-12 strongly recommended.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ce83c82866a5b48845f761
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
