DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T200000
UID:69dee07f4dacf581ff88d9b5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join the Tuesday chess club at\nGuildwood Library\n\, as we pl
 ay chess every Tuesday starting on\nMay 5\nth\n. Players of all strengths 
 and skill level are welcomed to participate in the club. Chess introductio
 n lessons are available for new players that are new to the game. The prog
 ram is for\nchildren ages 7+\, teens\, and adults\n. For More Information\
 , please call the Guildwood Library at 416-396-8872.\nDrop-In. No registra
 tion required.\nIf you identify as a person with a disability and require 
 an accessibility accommodation to participate in this program\, please con
 tact Accessibility Services by email\, accessibleservices@tpl.ca\, or voic
 email\, 416-393-7099\, to make a request. Please contact us at least three
  weeks in advance.
LOCATION:Guildwood\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dee07f4dacf581ff88d9b5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Girls Coding
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T130000
UID:69c1a19ab6c4ac1fedc7addc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program introduces children to beginner computer programm
 ing and fosters the development of essential STEM skills. Delivered in col
 laboration with Macaulay Centres for Children\, the initiative focuses on 
 promoting educational growth and enhancing future employment opportunities
 \, particularly for children in marginalized communities. Participants wil
 l engage in hands-on coding activities\, make new friends\, and have fun i
 n a supportive. Space is limited\, and advance registration with a commitm
 ent to attend the full session is required.
LOCATION:Woodview Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1a19ab6c4ac1fedc7addc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
