BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Game On: Building Life Skills Through Soccer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T170000
UID:69f1281b762d19c7d5106b9c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Coach and athlete Pepy Malonga shares essential life skills su
 ch as leadership\, teamwork\, communication\, and decision-making in a fun
  and relatable way through soccer and sports. Through interactive games\, 
 real-life examples\, and discussion\, participants connect their love of s
 port to valuable tools for life success on and off the field.\nFor childre
 n ages 6-12. This is a drop-in program. No registration is required\, but
  space is limited.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informati
 on on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publi
 c Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will
  only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation
 . Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed
  to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge St
 reet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f1281b762d19c7d5106b9c
